.TH smi-pki-start-intermediate-ca "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI PKI Command"
.SH NAME
smi-pki-start-intermediate-ca \- Create an Intermediate CA signed by the Root CA
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-pki-start-intermediate-ca
.I DIRECTORY ROOT_DOMAIN
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Creates the Intermediate CA (4096-bit) in \fIDIRECTORY\fB/ca\fR, signed by the Root CA of \fIROOT_DOMAIN\fR, never self-signed. Stored as \fI<root-domain>.intermediate.*\fR.
It is a thin command line wrapper over the matching function in the file based PKI library
\fBpki.sh\fR, so each step of building a CA and signing certificates can be run and inspected
on its own. All material is passed as file names; the command fails if the underlying OpenSSL
operation fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-pki-ca-create (1),
.BR smi-pki-create-domain-cert (1),
.BR openssl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Imre Tabur <imre.tabur@mail.ee>
